%% Two things, joined at the release channel they share: (1) how a change moves from a
%% contributor's first push through to a published package, and the surfaces (CLI, SDK,
%% API, MCP, Webhook) vibey-gh exposes that release automation through; and (2) the
%% vibey-skills product itself — its source modules and the two capability surfaces it
%% exposes on its own account, a CLI and a Python SDK, plus the marketplace manifest
%% Claude Code reads directly. vibey-skills has no HTTP API, MCP server, or webhook
%% endpoint of its own.
flowchart TD
    Dev[Contributor] -->|push| Topic[Topic branch]
    Topic -->|pull_request_target| BranchIntake[Branch intake]
    BranchIntake -->|opens draft PR| PR[Pull request]
    PR -->|push| develop[develop]

    Topic --> CLI[vibey-gh CLI]
    CLI --> Check[check]
    CLI --> Install[install]
    CLI --> Version[version]
    CLI --> MergeTrainCmd[merge-train]
    CLI --> Promote[promote]
    CLI --> Realign[Realign]

    Check --> Provenance[Provenance]
    Check --> CodeQL[CodeQL: Analyze Python]
    Provenance -->|required check| Gate{"PR Automation gate"}
    CodeQL -->|required check| Gate
    CIWorkflow[CI: Validate manifests and build] -->|required check| Gate
    Docs[Docs: Build docs strict] -->|required check| Gate
    PRAutomation[PR automation] -->|publishes| Gate

    Gate -->|green + approved| MergeTrain[Merge train]
    MergeTrain -->|squash merge| develop

    develop -->|push| ReleaseWorkflow[Release]
    ReleaseWorkflow -->|vibey-gh version --dev| TestPyPI[TestPyPI]
    TestPyPI -->|verify install| VerifyGate{Verify}

    VerifyGate --> PromoteWorkflow[Promote]
    PromoteWorkflow -->|content diff develop vs main| PromotePR[Promotion PR]
    PromotePR -->|rebase merge| main[main]

    main -->|push| ReleaseWorkflow
    ReleaseWorkflow -->|vibey-gh version| PyPI[PyPI]
    PyPI --> GitHubPages[GitHub Pages]
    ReleaseWorkflow -->|on a v* tag: tag, release, attach dist/*| GitHubRelease[GitHub Release]
    ReleaseWorkflow -->|workflow_run| GitHubReleaseWorkflow[github-release.yml]
    GitHubReleaseWorkflow -->|tag + release, no bump: expected failure| GitHubRelease
    GitHubReleaseWorkflow -->|workflow_run| ReleaseArtifacts[Release artifacts]
    ReleaseArtifacts -->|attaches dist/*| GitHubRelease

    main -->|realign| Realign
    Realign -->|fast-forward, only if trees match| develop

    subgraph Surfaces[vibey-gh capability surfaces]
        CLI
        SDK[SDK]
        API[API]
        MCP[MCP]
        Webhook[Webhook]
    end

    Registry[Capability registry] --> CLI
    Registry --> SDK
    Registry --> API
    Registry --> MCP
    Registry --> Webhook

    subgraph SecurityBoundary[Security Boundary]
        Fork[Fork PR] -.->|never trusted with write access| Gate
        AutomergeToken[AUTOMERGE_TOKEN] -->|admin role, required review bypass| MergeTrain
        AnthropicKey[ANTHROPIC_API_KEY] -->|scoped: no merge, no settings| CurrencyResearch[Currency research agent]
        CurrencyResearch -->|opens PR only| PR
        LocalFallback[Local review fallback: vibey-local runner + Ollama] -->|reviews only when the paid path returned no verdict| Gate
        LocalFallback -.->|trusted_only: fork PRs never reach the self-hosted runner| Fork
        LocalFallback -->|verdict labelled: gate - local fallback| MergeTrain
    end

    %% ---- The vibey-skills product itself: source modules and its own two surfaces ----
    subgraph Product[vibey-skills product — source modules & capability surfaces]
        SkillsTree["plugins/**: 127 plugin dirs, 644 SKILL.md"] --> Init["src/vibey_skills/__init__.py: iter_skills, plugins_root, marketplace_manifest"]
        Init --> SkillsCLI["vibey-skills CLI (cli.py)"]
        Init --> SkillsSDK["Python SDK: from vibey_skills import iter_skills, plugins_root"]
        SkillsTree --> MarketplaceJSON[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json"]

        SkillsCLI --> ListCmd[list]
        SkillsCLI --> InstallCmd[install]
        SkillsCLI --> PathCmd[path]
        SkillsCLI --> MarketCmd[marketplace]
        SkillsCLI --> IndexCmd["index build / inspect"]
        SkillsCLI --> SearchCmd[search]
        SkillsCLI --> PacketCmd[packet]
        SkillsCLI --> EvaluateCmd[evaluate]

        InstallCmd -->|copy, or --link symlink; cp -n semantics| ClaudeSkillsDir["~/.claude/skills"]
        IndexCmd --> ContextEngine["context_engine.py: SQLite FTS5 index"]
        SearchCmd --> ContextEngine
        PacketCmd --> ContextEngine
        EvaluateCmd --> ContextEngine

        ValidateManifests["tools/validate_manifests.py: manifest & frontmatter validator"]
        CheckLinks["tools/check_links.py: hermetic link checker"]
        SkillsTree --> ValidateManifests
        MarketplaceJSON --> ValidateManifests
    end

    CIWorkflow -->|invokes| ValidateManifests
    CIWorkflow -->|invokes| CheckLinks

    SkillsTree --> Wheel["hatchling force-include: plugins/ -> wheel"]
    Wheel --> PyPI
    PyPI -->|pip install / uvx / uv tool install| SkillsCLI
    MarketplaceJSON -.->|"/plugin marketplace add — read directly, no CLI or SDK involved"| ClaudeCodeMarketplace[Claude Code]

    %% vibey-skills exposes exactly two capability surfaces of its own: the CLI and the
    %% Python SDK. There is no HTTP API, MCP server, or webhook endpoint in this product —
    %% the API/MCP/Webhook surfaces earlier in this diagram belong to vibey-gh, the
    %% separate release-automation dependency, not to vibey-skills.
